{% doc %}
  Placeholder rows for the search panel's idle column.

  Shown when the merchant has not chosen any suggestion products yet — in the
  theme editor, where it lets them judge the panel's layout before configuring
  it, and on a live storefront, where an empty column under a "Suggestion
  products" heading looks like something that failed to load.

  The copy is deliberately, visibly an example. `Example product` and a round
  `$19.99` are Shopify's own onboarding convention: a customer who sees them
  knows immediately that nothing real is there, which an invented product name
  and a plausible price would not. The rows are not links for the same reason —
  there is nowhere honest for them to go.

  ## Kept in step with the real card

  This deliberately reuses `snippets/predictive-search-card.liquid`'s classes
  rather than its markup: `.search-card`, `.search-card__media`,
  `.search-card__body`, `.search-card__title`, `.search-card__meta` and
  `.search-card__price` all come from `assets/search.css`, so the typography,
  the 64px media tile, its 1:1 ratio and the row rhythm are the card's, not a
  second set that can drift from it. Only the contents differ.

  @param {number} [count] - How many rows. Default 3, the length of a typical
    suggestion list

  @example
    {% render 'predictive-search-placeholder', count: 3 %}
{% enddoc %}

{%- liquid
  assign placeholder_count = count | default: 3
  assign placeholder_title = 'search.placeholder.title' | t
  assign placeholder_meta = 'search.placeholder.meta' | t
  assign placeholder_price = 1999 | money
-%}

<ul class="search-group__items" role="list" data-placeholder-group>
  {%- for index in (1..placeholder_count) -%}
    {%- comment -%}
      A different mark per row. Three identical drawings read as one image
      repeated by mistake; three different ones read as a list.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- liquid
      assign marks = 'product-apparel-1,product-apparel-2,product-apparel-3' | split: ','
      assign mark_index = forloop.index0 | modulo: marks.size
      assign mark = marks[mark_index]
    -%}

    <li class="search-card-item" data-placeholder>
      <span class="search-card search-card--placeholder">
        <span class="search-card__media" aria-hidden="true">
          {{ mark | placeholder_svg_tag: 'search-card__placeholder-svg' }}
        </span>

        <span class="search-card__body">
          <span class="search-card__title">{{ placeholder_title }}</span>
          <span class="search-card__meta">{{ placeholder_meta }}</span>

          <span class="search-card__footer">
            <span class="search-card__price">
              <span class="search-card__price-current">{{ placeholder_price }}</span>
            </span>
          </span>
        </span>
      </span>
    </li>
  {%- endfor -%}
</ul>
